+# Send pickup reminders by SMS
+
+For whoever proposes switching pickup reminders to email to save the SMS cost, or changes `larder/reminders.py`.
+Reminders go by SMS, about 40 euros a month, because when they went by email for three months twice as many pantry
+orders were never picked up.
+
+## Context
+
+The day before pickup, larder reminds each member of their pantry order's pickup slot. SMS costs about 40 euros a
+month and email costs nothing, so switching keeps being proposed: issue 52 was the third proposal in one year.
+
+The pantry tried it. From April to June 2025 reminders went by email. The email provider reported that 34% of the
+reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Many members share one
+phone across the family and never check email; an SMS they see. Each missed pickup is a packed bag whose fresh food
+is thrown away at closing time. Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by
+August.
+
+Two forces judge the options: a member must see the reminder, since a missed pickup wastes the food packed for it;
+and the pantry runs on a small budget, so a channel that costs nothing is preferred when it reaches members as well.
+
+## Options
+
+- **Email**: free, and `remind` already sends it when `CHANNEL` is not `"sms"`; lost on the first force, since in the
+  2025 trial a third of the emails went unopened and missed pickups doubled, to 13%.
+- **SMS**: chosen.
+
+## Decision
+
+Pickup reminders go by SMS, because it is the channel members see: missed pickups stay at 6%, against 13% by email.
+The 40 euros a month costs less than the food a doubled rate of missed pickups throws away. The maintainer confirmed
+it when closing issue 52.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Members see their reminder and missed pickups stay near 6% of pantry orders. The pantry pays about 40 euros a month for
+SMS. A proposal to save that cost needs evidence that the new channel keeps missed pickups near 6%; what would change
+the answer is members reading email, not email's price. Switching back is one constant, `CHANNEL` in
+`larder/reminders.py`.
